  "body": "Branch carries upstream/main a9ec0982 (merged twice, no rebase; it trial-merges clean with 683802be, a verify-only change). Fork synced at v0.18.0. Reworked onto main's EDM designs (wire post #533, serves law #1232/#1266); decisions in `docs/decisions/542-sinker-iso-post.md` under \"2026-11-12 - rework onto main's EDM designs\".\n\n## What changed\n- **`assets/posts/sinker-iso.cps`** (\"Sinker EDM (ISO)\", `posting::SINKER_POSTS`): a generic ISO-style sinker post. It writes the RS-274 words itself (G0 with changed axis words, G90, the setup's work offset, `( )` comments) and takes every EDM-specific code from the machine's `edm.codes` (#290 D5): `metric` / `inch`, `pickup` (`{tool}`), `reference` (`{offset}`), `condition` (`{id}`), `depth` (`{z}`, optional `{f}`), `end`. A missing code, a placeholder the post does not fill, or one with no value is refused by name. A burn posts as rapid approach, the `depth` code, rapid retract; a feed with X/Y travel, a feed up, an arc, a cycle, compensation, an rpm or a coolant ask is refused by name.\n- **Refused by name, never posted silently wrong (new in the rework):** a condition the machine's `edm.conditions` does not list (exact id, as the table writes it); an orbit (#544 - its explicit moves are what the stock sim judged, never swapped for the control's orbit word, even a listed one); a Sinker Side Burn (#545).\n- **Codes: main's store and validator.** Main's `Machine.edm_codes` and `post::machine::edm_codes` (lowercase names, printable text, `CODE_MAX`, no brackets). The PR's own `Edm.codes` store and looser parser are dropped; `SINKER_CODES` stays as the list of names the sinker post reads, pinned to pass main's law.\n- **serves: main's manifest and door.** `serves = [\"sinker_edm\"];` and the registry (`BUILTINS`, `SINKER_POSTS`, `post_serves`, `default_post_for`, `post_offer`) beside main's wire entries. The PR's engine `serves_gate` is dropped. Main's `posting_family::edm_at_post` (\"no post for a sinker EDM machine yet (#542)\") is retired: every writer's `posting_serves::refusal` right after it refuses any post that does not serve a sinker, by name.\n- **`PARAM SinkerCondition`** (was `EdmCondition` in this PR): main's `EdmCondition` is the wire section's word and main's engine refuses it through any script without `wireEdm`. The sinker gets its own word and an engine door beside the wire one: `SinkerCondition` through a script whose `serves` does not name `sinker_edm` is refused by name. The wire door is unchanged.\n- **Stream PARAMs** (`crates/app/src/posting_edm.rs`): `SinkerCondition`, `ElectrodePickup` for a Sinker Burn and a Sinker Side Burn; `EdmOrbit` / `EdmOrbitRadius` for an orbit.\n- **Mirror:** `post::machine::mirror` writes main's `edm: {codes, awt}`; a sinker's adds `orbits`, `pickup`, `conditions` in the same object (mm). One `script_props` `edm` key (main's pass-through); the post reads only words and ids from it, so no unit scaling or raw re-parse is needed.\n- **Recorded harness:** main's `recorded/mod.rs` (`machine_of(case)` + mirrored temp `.mch`), with `verdict_on` / `compare` added for the sinker burn case.\n- Docs: `assets/machines/AGENTS.md` (`edm.codes` under main's validator), `docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md` (the sinker row beside main's wire row), the user guide's EDM pages. `assets/posts/AGENTS.md` and `PROCESS_VERSION` are main's: the PR now changes no process file, so no bump.\n- Fixture dialect `crates/app/tests/edm/sinker-iso-dialect.mch`: SYNTHETIC invented words, not any control's.\n- MCP: no new command; the existing post selection and posting tools address the new registry name.\n\n## Goldens / output\n- Byte-identical after the rework: `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/sinker-iso/sinker_burn_cavity.nc`, `sinker_burn_program.nc`, `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/sinker-iso/sinker_burn_cavity.nc`.\n- Changed form: the nine recorded mill-case refusals (`recorded/golden/sinker-iso/*.refusal`) - from the dropped engine gate's stop to the script's counted warnings (still refused, never released). Main's two new cases (`css_then_live`, `live_then_stop`) recorded in the same form. Line-by-line explanation in the rework comment.\n\n## How tested\nPinning tests:\n- `crates/post/tests/script_sinker_iso.rs`: `the_sinker_burn_posts_to_its_golden_against_the_fixture_dialect`, `every_missing_sinker_code_refuses_the_post_by_name`, `a_code_naming_a_placeholder_the_post_does_not_fill_refuses_by_name`, `an_orbit_is_refused_by_name_even_one_the_machine_lists`, `a_sinker_side_burn_is_refused_by_name`, `a_condition_the_machine_does_not_list_is_refused_by_name`, `a_mill_post_on_a_sinker_and_the_sinker_post_on_a_mill_are_refused` (fanuc, haas, tormach-plasma, fanuc-lathe, wire-iso on the sinker burn; sinker-iso on a VMC and on no machine), `a_wear_layered_burn_posts_each_layer_as_the_depth_code` (#546), `a_feed_with_xy_travel_or_an_rpm_is_refused_by_name`, `sinker_burn_cavity` and the 11 recorded cases.\n- Unit: `post::machine::edm_codes::the_sinker_names_pass_the_one_law_and_a_bad_sinker_code_refuses_by_name`.\n- `crates/app/tests/sinker_burn.rs`: `the_sinker_burn_posts_through_the_generic_sinker_post_to_its_golden`, `a_missing_sinker_code_refuses_the_post_by_name`, `a_mill_post_on_a_sinker_machine_is_still_refused`, `an_orbit_burn_and_a_side_burn_say_their_sinker_params_in_the_stream`, the MCP test (now the serves door's refusal).\n- Wire keeps posting on a wire machine: main's `wire_post.rs` and `script_wire_iso.rs` unchanged and green; `wire_post::a_sinker_setup_is_still_refused_at_post_by_name` pins the wire post (and every cutting post) refused on a sinker.\n- `conformance.rs`: `every_sinker_post_refuses_every_mill_golden_by_name`, registry and extension pins list both EDM posts.\n\nGate on head 5ee6e12e (worktree target, sccache):\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post` (lib + every suite, incl. `script_sinker_iso` 21, `script_wire_iso` 11, `recorded_streams` 12): green.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app` --test conformance, plasma_post, plasma_post_refusals, post_serves_kind, post_serves_plasma, posting, sinker_burn, sinker_burn_held, sinker_orbit, sinker_side, sinker_wear, solid_law_goldens, wire_contour, wire_post, wire_readers, wire_verify, smoothing, edm_machine, edm_conditions, mcp_edit_machine: 20 binaries green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green on 5ee6e12e - post suites (6 s) and app suites (1171 s), 19.6 min wall, 0 failed (also green on 0751b16b before main moved).\n\n## Not exercised\n- **Not exercised on a real EDM control** (#290 D10). The dialect, condition and part are synthetic; a user fills `edm.codes` from the control's manual and dry-runs before any burn.\n- The orbit and side-burn refusals are pinned on the post from hand-edited streams and on the app at the stream level; no orbit/side program was posted end-to-end through `post_setup` (the fixture cavity is sized to a straight burn, so the stock sim would convict either first).\n- No Hub run. No library sinker machine yet (#1135).\n\nChangelog: Sinker EDM: a generic ISO-style sinker post (\"Sinker EDM (ISO)\", serves sinker_edm) posts a straight Sinker Burn with every EDM code (unit, pickup, reference, condition, burn to depth, end) read from the machine's edm.codes; a missing code, a condition the machine does not list, an orbit and a Sinker Side Burn are refused by name (#542)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #542\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
